{"name":"Guns N’ Roses","hex":"#ff0077","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"guns","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of gun"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Well-developed muscles of the upper arm, especially the biceps and triceps."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guns"},{"term":"roses","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of rose"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of rose"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roses"}],"entries":[{"title":"Guns N' Roses","blocks":[{"text":"Guns N' Roses is an American hard rock band formed in Los Angeles, California, in 1985 from L.A. Guns and Hollywood Rose. After signing with Geffen Records in 1986, the band's \"classic\" lineup featured vocalist Axl Rose, lead guitarist Slash, rhythm guitarist Izzy Stradlin, bassist Duff McKagan, and drummer Steven Adler."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/GNR_Belgrade_2025_05_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-GNR_Belgrade_2025_05_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guns_N'_Roses","wikidata":"Q11895"},{"title":"Gun","blocks":[{"text":"A gun is a device that propels a projectile using pressure or explosive force. The projectiles are typically solid, but can also be pressurized liquid, or gas. Solid projectiles may be free-flying or tethered. A large-caliber gun is also called a cannon, while a hand-held gun may be called a firearm. Guns were designed as weapons for military use, and then found use in hunting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/SIG_Pro_by_Augustas_Didzgalvis.jpg/330px-SIG_Pro_by_Augustas_Didzgalvis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gun","wikidata":"Q110155210"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose","wikidata":"Q34687"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/65/Gnr_orig_lineup.jpg/330px-Gnr_orig_lineup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/65/Gnr_orig_lineup.jpg/330px-Gnr_orig_lineup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The original lineup of Guns N' Roses in March 1985. From left to right: Rob Gardner, Izzy Stradlin, Axl Rose, Tracii Guns and Ole Beich.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGnr_orig_lineup.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a4/Guns-N-Roses-1987.jpg/330px-Guns-N-Roses-1987.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a4/Guns-N-Roses-1987.jpg/330px-Guns-N-Roses-1987.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Guns N' Roses classic lineup, from left to right, Izzy Stradlin, Steven Adler, Axl Rose, Duff McKagan, & Slash","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGuns-N-Roses-1987.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Slashvr.jpg/500px-Slashvr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_